            <h2>About Universiti Malaysia Terengganu</h2>
            <p>
                Universiti Malaysia Terengganu (UMT) is a public university located in Kuala Nerus, Terengganu, Malaysia. It began as Universiti Pertanian Malaysia's Centre for Fisheries and Marine Science in 1979, providing facilities for students and lecturers from the Fisheries and Marine Science programs to conduct practical sessions and research.
            </p>
            <p>
                Over the decades, the institution evolved from a university college (KUSTEM) into a full-fledged public university in February 2007. Today, UMT is nationally and internationally recognized as Malaysia's premier marine-focused university, specializing in marine science, aquatic resources, oceanography, and sustainable environmental management.
            </p>
            <p>
                Situated along the scenic coast of the South China Sea, the campus offers state-of-the-art research vessels, marine hatcheries, and modern computing laboratories that support innovative teaching, learning, and community engagement.
            </p>
        </article>

